+- Typed image placeholders (merged upstream implementation with local policy integration) are real 1x1 zero-initialized images, distinct from Vulkan native-null descriptors. Sampling and fetches observe the chosen heap format, valid extent and fixed sample count (4 for MS heaps); image size/sample queries, comparison sampling, out-of-range access, storage writes and atomics do not acquire native-null semantics. Storage descriptors in a heap alias its placeholder and writes may survive later draws. A missing format, sample, portability-array or atomic feature leaves that heap unavailable and its first null use fails explicitly. `RequiresValidImages` continues to reject zero guest descriptors and zero Vulkan views; `NativeNull` still requires the actually enabled robustness2 feature. `TypedPlaceholders` has a separate request17/cache28 identity. No bare zero Vulkan image view is used in the fallback.
+
+- Single-sample depth/stencil maintenance clears retain the upstream resident-image and HTILE-clear tracking. This does not establish a general guest depth-plane import, CPU-write invalidation or writeback contract. Grouped multisample draws continue to reject Z consumption and non-equivalent maintenance clears; their supported stencil path explicitly refreshes and writes back the guest S8 plane.
+- Graphics pipeline libraries are selected before shader preparation and use fixed push slots. The explicit `APS5_ENABLE_SAMPLE_GROUPS` profile retains its render-pass and programmed sample-location path; it does not enable graphics pipeline libraries. Request17/cache28 and the complete PSO key distinguish these layouts.
